    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0579" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2075.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1911</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 621.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to the
                    Department herewith, for its information, in connection with the dangers to
                    which it seemed Americans and American property would be exposed in the event of
                    a mob outbreak in this city, a copy of my note to the Mexican <pb facs="0580"
                        n="498" xml:id="pg498"/> foreign office in which it is intimated to the
                    Mexican Government that unless adequate protection were afforded that Government
                    would be held liable for all loss of life and damage to property.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d744-a1.xml" xpointer="d744-a1"/>
            </div>
